---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import MailLink from '../components/MailLink.astro';
---
<Base title="Rooted in the Land — a men's writing retreat, January 2027"
      ogImage="/img/og-retreat-1200x630.jpg"
      ogImageAlt="A weathered cabin among bare winter trees at sunrise, snow on the ground."
      description="A men's writing retreat inspired by Wendell Berry. January 15–17, 2027, at the Bergamo Center in Ohio. Co-led by Brian Mueller and Tom Sparough.">

  <section class="hero hero-retreat">
    <img class="hero-img" src="/img/retreat-band-1456.webp"
         srcset="/img/retreat-band-700.webp 700w, /img/retreat-band-1000.webp 1000w, /img/retreat-band-1456.webp 1456w"
         sizes="100vw" width="1456" height="470" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="hero-veil hero-veil-strong"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow">January 15–17, 2027 · Bergamo Center, Ohio</div>
      <h1>Rooted in the Land</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">A men's writing retreat inspired by Wendell Berry. Join us for a
         weekend of reflection, fraternity and renewal, as we write our way toward a deeper
         belonging.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-light" href="#register">Registration</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ondark" href="#is-it-for-me">Is this for me?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="stack stack-m measure">
      <div class="eyebrow">The weekend</div>
      <h2>Writing our way toward belonging</h2>
      <p>This year our circle of brotherhood draws its inspiration from the poetry and agrarian
         wisdom of Wendell Berry. Together we explore stillness, nature, and the sacredness of
         everyday life, and we reflect on our relationship with the land we live upon.</p>
      <p>The quest is to use writing as a vehicle to rediscover the divine presence in our own
         stories.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-poem" id="is-it-for-me">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="stack stack-m measure">
      <div class="eyebrow">Before you talk yourself out of it</div>
      <h2>Is this retreat for me?</h2>
      <p><b>You don't have to think of yourself as a poet or a writer to get a great deal from
         this weekend.</b> It is open to men of every level of experience — complete novice to
         published author. You can write poetry, a series of journal entries, or some combination
         of the two. The focus is the spiritual journey, not the craft.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="stack stack-m measure">
      <div class="eyebrow">The shape of it</div>
      <h2>Multiple Writing Experiences</h2>
      <p>Each session opens with poetic inspiration from Wendell Berry and leads into a writing
         prompt. We gather as a large group, spend one-on-one time with another participant, and
         meet in small council circles where sharing your work is optional but deeply encouraged.</p>
      <p>Around the writing there is evening social time, optional morning prayer, an outdoor
         wandering or an indoor rest, and an open mic before we close on Sunday.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="arrival"><b>Friday arrival.</b> Doors from 4:00 p.m., rooms ready by 5:00,
       dinner at 6:00. The first session begins at about 7:00.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stack stack-m measure">
        <div class="eyebrow">Where you'll stay</div>
        <h2>The Bergamo Center</h2>
        <p>A hundred and fifty acres of forest, field and pond, close to the Dayton airport
           and yours to wander.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="facts">
        <div><dt>Your room</dt><dd>Single occupancy, private bathroom. No roommates, no negotiating.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Meals</dt><dd>Every meal, from Friday dinner through Sunday lunch. Dietary needs accommodated.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The grounds</dt><dd>150 acres of forest, fields and a pond, made for quiet walking.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Getting there</dt><dd>4400 Shakertown Road, Dayton, OH 45430 — close to Dayton airport. If you fly, we'll try to arrange a volunteer to collect you.</dd></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="stack stack-m measure">
      <div class="eyebrow">Your guides</div>
      <h2>Who is carrying the content</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="guides">
      <article class="guide">
        <h3>Brian Mueller</h3>
        <p>Graphic designer, presence guide, and poet with ten self-published volumes of poetry.
           He has co-led this retreat for a decade.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="/about">About Brian</a> · <a href="https://brianspoems.com">brianspoems.com</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="guide">
        <h3>Tom Sparough</h3>
        <p>Author of seven of his own eclectic books and one full-length play, and a freelance
           content editor.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="https://spacepainter.com">spacepainter.com</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-poem" id="register">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="stack stack-m measure">
      <div class="eyebrow">Registration</div>
      <h2>Opening soon</h2>
      <p>Fifty places. Registration will open on this page, and we will announce it by email and
         through Illuman. We have not fixed the opening date yet — if you would like to be told,
         send the email below and you will be.</p>
      <div class="facts facts-tight">
        <div><dt>Dates</dt><dd>Friday, January 15 – Sunday, January 17, 2027. Arrive from 4:00 p.m., rooms ready by 5:00, dinner at 6:00, and our first session at about 7:00. We close after lunch on Sunday.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>$350 through December 1, 2026. $400 after that. Your room and every meal are included.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>If the fee is a barrier</dt><dd>Assistance is available, quietly and without explanation. Write to us before you register.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>If your plans change</dt><dd>Through December 1, 2026 we refund in full less a $35 administrative fee. From December 2 to January 1, half. After January 1 the Bergamo Center bills us for your room and meals either way, so we cannot refund — but write to us if something serious happens.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Access needs</dt><dd>Tell us when you register, or before. We pass dietary and accessibility needs to the Bergamo Center ten days ahead.</dd></div>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <MailLink class="btn" user="brian" domain="b-drive.us"
                  label="Email me about registration"
                  subject="Rooted in the Land 2027"
                  body={"I'd like to know when registration opens for Rooted in the Land, January 15\u201317, 2027.\n\nName:\n"}
          ><a class="btn" href="/contact">Email me about registration</a></MailLink>
      </div>
      <p class="small">That button opens a pre-addressed email in your mail app — you still have to
         send it. Brian keeps the list himself and writes back to everyone on it when registration
         opens. It is not a booking and it does not hold a place.</p>
      <p class="small">Questions in the meantime: Brian Mueller —
         <MailLink user="brian" domain="b-drive.us"><a href="/contact">write to Brian</a></MailLink>
         · Tom Sparough —
         <MailLink user="tsparough" domain="gmail.com"><a href="/contact">write to Brian, who will pass it on</a></MailLink></p>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="colophon-note">
      <p>This writing retreat is inspired by and celebrates the work of Wendell Berry. Permission
         to use excerpts from his work has been graciously granted by his publisher, Counterpoint
         Press. Please note that Mr. Berry has not endorsed or sponsored this event.</p>
      <p><em>Rooted in the Land</em> is an event of Ohio Illuman, a chapter of
         <a href="https://illuman.org">Illuman</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
